      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The reason you gave is about scheduling. It isn't a clinical reason for giving 50 mg. Amlodipine at five times the maximum dose could cause profound hypotension and shock. Because its half-life is long (30\u201350 hours), the effects could last for days. A family visit or evening rounds can't offset that risk.\n\nI can do any of these right away:\n- **Enter a standard dose:** 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, with a note asking for blood pressure review at evening rounds.\n- **Help with the actual goal:** If blood pressure needs more control than 10 mg gives, I can enter amlodipine 10 mg plus a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. You would choose the agent.\n- **Escalate:** If you think 50 mg is warranted, please talk to pharmacy or the attending first. Once they've approved it, the order can go through whatever override process your hospital requires.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
